Short:        A small assembler example for beginners.
Author:       davsjo@algonet.se (David Sjölin)
Uploader:     davsjo algonet se (David Sjölin)
Type:         dev/asm
Architecture: m68k-amigaos

Long: This archive contains the assembler source to
a small program which writes out the argument that
you write after the program name. Not much of a
program but if you try to learn how to code assembler
you'll probably find it educating.

Requirements: An Amiga, preferably with OS3.X.
(Haven't tried it on earlier models).

Legal Stuff: This program is of course Freeware since I
can't really stop you from using the source. But if you
make anything useful of it please send me the result.
